"# }) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** a server that answers `/api/items?page=…` with a list of items.")
            CodeBlock(#"type Item { id: String, name: String }

api Catalog(base: "/api") {
    get items(page: Number = 1) -> [Item]
}

page Items(path: "/items", title: "Items", description: "Everything, a page at a time.") {
    state page = 1
    resource list = Catalog.items(page: page, paginate: .page)
    Heading("Items").h1
    for item in list.items by item.id { Text(item.name) }
    if list.hasMore {
        Button("Load more", disabled: list.pending) { on click { list.loadMore() } }
    }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("The page shows the first page of items and a **Load more** button. Each press adds the next page beneath what is there, without losing the reader's place, and the button goes away once there is nothing more.\n\n- `Catalog` [describes the service](/learn/15-data#describe-a-service-with-api): its `items` endpoint takes a `page` and returns a list of `Item`.\n- The resource calls it with `paginate: .page`, which gives it `.items`, `.loadMore()` and `.hasMore` ([Load results a page at a time](/learn/15-data#load-results-a-page-at-a-time)).\n- `list.items` is every item loaded so far, so the `for` lists them all and `item.name` is checked against `Item`.\n- `list.loadMore()` moves `page` on by one and asks for the next page, as a refresh: the items already shown stay while it runs.\n- `list.pending` is true while a request runs, so the button cannot ask twice. `list.hasMore` turns false when a page comes back empty, and the button goes.")

    }
}
